<title>USA: US banks free reserves $1.239 bln Jan 15 rvd 2 wks.</title>
<headline>US banks free reserves $1.239 bln Jan 15 rvd 2 wks.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. commercial banks had revised free reserves of $1.239 billion per day in the two weeks ended January 15, versus revised free reserves of $1.389 billion in the previous two-week period, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>Seasonal borrowings were $18 million versus $64 million a day. Extended credits were nil.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
